And certain materials are inherently immune to decay.  Silver,
mithril, bone.  All unicorn horns are fooproof because they are
made of bone, etc.

> > 3.  Is there any way to remove rust, corrosion, rot from armor?

Same as with a weapon, confused scroll.  Not an option for illiterate
conduct.  So go with armor that is made of a material that starts
immune ro decay.  Mithril, silver, dragon scales.

> > I've only found a few +0 dwarvish mithril coats as the best body armor
> > (in terms of overall AC).  Would it be worth it to replace the gray
> > dragon scales with the dwarvish mithril coat
>
> Put that dragon scale on you with no other armour, then read a
> non-cursed scroll of enchant armour (UNconfused) for a pleasant
> surprise. If you have no enchant armour at the moment, yes switch to
> dwarvish mithril until you do, so keep the scales around.

The standard tradeoffs of NetHack.  There are several correct answers.
With illiterate cinduct you have no way to repair damage so solve
that problem by using immune materials for some armor and having
spares for other armor.

> > I'd only get a boost of -3 to
> > my AC (go down to -1 total).  If not, how about if I locate a +4
> > dwarvish mitril coat?  Will the boost of -7 (go down to -5 total) be
> > good?
>
> You can just go "locate" a +4 mithril? I bow before you. Yes, a boost
> of -7 will be a huge difference.

That's the tradeoff.  If you stay in the dungeon long enough you
will have plenty of dragon scales, but I don't ever recall a dragon
scale that wasn't +0 when I lifted it from the dragon's corpse.  If
you stay in the dungeon long enough (especially the mines) you will
have *plenty* of dwarvish and elvish mithril mail to chose from, and
some will be nicely enchanted.

Sounds to me like you should keep a stash near an altar, go with the
best enchanted armor you have at the moment, take all loot to your
stash, and be ready to switch armor if some nice monster leaves you
better stuff in their will.

Characters who read scrolls or use wishes generally end up with a
few standard combinations of armor.  GSDM or SDSM, a source of MR
or magic resistance, a cloak with MC=3, speed boots, etc.  Doing a
conduct with neither scrolls nor wishes, you will not end up with a
collection like that, and that means you need to judge your items
on the fly.  I suspect that different parts of the game will give
different answers.  Gray scales for a while plus a nice cloak,
highly enchanted mithril for a while thanks to a monster tough to
kill plus an MR cloak.

